President Trump says he looks forward to  working with Frances newly elected  leader Emmanuel macron the centrist  scored a resounding victory over far  right candidate marine lepen he won  about two-thirds of the votes cast at 39  years old McCrone becomes france's  youngest head of state since Napoleon  this morning he joined France's current  president at a ceremony make marking the  end of World War two in Europe  mark Phillips is in Paris with what the  election results mean for France's  future mark good morning good morning  well president Trump may have  congratulated the new president-elect of  France to Immanuel back crawl but during  the campaign he actually tweeted that he  thought the various terrorist attacks in  France would help his right-wing  opponent marine lepen  he was wrong the winners strode on stage  to give his victory speech accompanied  by Beethoven's Ode to Joy the European  anthem the loser tried to dance her  blues away - I love rock and roll she  couldn't have loved the numbers Emmanuel  macron is a 39 year old former  investment banker who had briefly been a  cabinet minister but had never run for  office before with both the left and the  right of French politics rejected by the  voters he came up the middle in a 66 to  34 win that can only be called a  landslide many thick black Ross said he  understood the anger of those who had  supported his far right-wing opponent  and would work for them - viva la  république but it's hard to see how the  principles of marine lepen nationalist  anti-immigration National Front can be  accommodated by a factor of two to one  the French had chosen macros moderation  overlap ends extremism in the French  system voters are given two ballots each  with one candidate's name on it they  vote with one and throw the other way  trash bags across France were full of  rejected scraps of paper with marine  lepen name on the news is not all good  for Emmanuel macron he appeared at a VE  Day commemoration with the outgoing  president Francois alone and he now  inherits all the problems that undermine  the alone presidency Emmanuel macron ran  his campaign on a completely different  set of policies to Donald Trump and to  his opponent marine lepen  she campaigned on protectionism closing  borders he argued for an  internationalist approach and economic  reform and Gail he won all right Mark  Phillips reporting in Paris thank you  Mark
 

